Q: Execute OdbcConnection within a TransactionScope but avoid automatic enlistment A: <p><code>OdbcConncetion.Open()</code> auto-enlist into the ambient <code>TransactionScope</code>. The Cache ODBC driver has no distributed transaction (MSTDTC) support, so it blows up with <code>HYCOO Driver not capable</code>. Wrap the ODBC part in a nested <code>TransactionScope(TransactionScopeOption.Suppress)</code>. That drops the ambient transaction just for that block, so the connection doesn't try to enlist, while your outer scope (around the <code>SQLConnection</code>) keeps working normally:</p>
<pre><code>using (var outerScope = new TransactionScope(...))
{
    // SqlConnection stuff, still part of the ambient transaction

    using (var suppressScope = new TransactionScope(TransactionScopeOption.Suppress))
    {
        using (var conn = new OdbcConnection(connString))
        {
            conn.Open();
            // your SELECT, no enlistment
        }
        suppressScope.Complete();
    }

    outerScope.Complete();
}
</code></pre>
